  "evaluation": "Good quantitative thresholds documented."
}"}

{"plan_objective_id": 4, "updated_plan_objective_json": "{
  "id": 4,
  "objective": "Research design implications for base machine to support future multi-laser upgrade",
  "rationale": "Have absorptivity data for aluminium at different wavelengths, DAM system architecture details, beam delivery specifications. Can synthesize design implications.",
  "status": "completed",
  "result": "AlSi12 absorptivity: 48% at 450nm, 26% at 808nm, 19% at 1060nm. DAM uses fibre-coupled diode arrays on gantry. DLAH/DPM uses 450nm melting + 915nm heating. F-theta lens specs and scanner architecture documented.",
  "evaluation": "Sufficient to synthesize design recommendations."
}"}

